# Line endings are a correctness concern here, not a style one
# (proposal/windows-support.md §3).
#
# Line 1: every checkout is LF, on every platform. Without it,
# Git-for-Windows' default `core.autocrlf=true` rewrites all 98 corpus
# goldens and every fixture at checkout, and the byte-identity gate fails
# wholesale.
#
# Line 2: belt and braces — the byte-identity corpus is exempt from any
# filter, ever. Its `.js` goldens are compared byte-for-byte against fresh
# compiler output, so no filter may ever touch them.
#
# Line 3: the same exemption for the split-emission fixture and its goldens
# (proposal/bundle-splitting.md S2), compared the same byte-for-byte way.
* text=auto eol=lf
vilan/test/** -text
crates/vilan-cli/tests/split/** -text
